==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ang|beoran}}

===Etymology===
{{root|ang|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*beran}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*beraną}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*bʰéreti}}.

Cognate with {{cog|ofs|bera}}, {{cog|osx|beran}}, {{cog|odt|beran}}, {{cog|goh|beran}}, {{cog|non|bera}}, {{cog|got|𐌱𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌰𐌽}}. The Indo-European root was also the source of {{cog|sga|biru}}, {{cog|grc|φέρω}}, {{cog|la|ferre}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|be+ran}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb}}

# to [[carry]], [[bear]], [[hold]]
#* '''late 10th century''', [[w:Ælfric of Eynsham|Ælfric]], [https://archive.org/details/aelfricslivesof01aelf/page/220/mode/2up?q= "Chair of Saint Peter"]
#*: {{quote|ang|...þā læġ þǣr sum creopere lama fram cildhāde sē wæs dæġhwāmlīce '''ġeboren''' tō þām beorhtan ġete þæt hē ælmessan underfencge æt þām infarendum...|Then lay there a cripple, lame from childhood, who was daily '''carried''' to the 'Beautiful' Gate, that he might receive alms from those entering.}}
#* '''c. 992''', [[w:Ælfric of Eynsham|Ælfric]], [https://books.google.com/books?id=2xobVW92JLcC&pg=PA432 "The Nativity of St. Clement the Martyr"]
#*: {{quote|ang|Þā sē enġel ġelǣhte hine be þām feaxe and hine '''bær''' tō Babylōne.|Then the angel grabbed him by the hair and '''carried''' him to Babylon.}}
#* '''late 10th century''', [[w:Ælfric of Eynsham|Ælfric]], [https://books.google.com/books?id=2xobVW92JLcC&pg=PA254 "On the Greater Litany"]
#*: {{quote|ang|Sē rīċa and sē þearfa sind weġfērende on þisse weorolde. Sē rīċa '''birþ''' māre þonne hē behōfiġe tō his formetum, sē ōðer '''birþ''' ǣmtiġne pusan. For þȳ sċeal sē rīċa dǣlan his byrðenne wiþ þone þearfan: þonne wanaþ hē þā byrðenne his synna, and þām þearfan ġehilpþ.|The rich and the poor are both wayfarers in this world. The rich '''carry''' more than they need for the journey, while the poor '''hold''' an empty sack. That's why the rich should share their burden with the poor. That way they can lighten the burden of their sins, and help the poor.}}
# to [[wear]]
# to [[sustain]], [[support]]
# to bring forth, [[produce]], give birth
#* '''late 9th century''', [https://books.google.com/books?id=xBNXAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA56 translation] of [[w:Orosius|Orosius']] ''History Against the Pagans''
#*: {{quote|ang|On þām dagum wæs Alexander '''ġeboren''' on Crēcum.|At that time, Alexander was '''born''' in Greece.}}

